  2407	place where a threshold $N_0$ could enter the algorithm is the small-$N$ branch, and FACTOR removes it by alternating trial division with SPLIT
  2408	step by step (Algorithm~\ref{alg:factor}, step~3). This costs at most a factor~$2$ in expected time. So even if some constant behind
